      "title": "Home sales hit 16-year low in October amid soaring mortgage rates",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/12/home-sales-october-low",
      "description": "<p>Sales of built units fell to 3.75m in October, down by 8.8% from last year, with mortgage rates at nearly three-year high</p><p>US existing home sales hit a 16-year low in October as buyers were driven away by high <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/money/mortgage-rates\">mortgage rates</a> and rising inflation, according to new data released on Wednesday.</p><p>Sales of already built units dropped to 3.75m in October, down by 8.8% from last year, the National Association of Realtors (NAR) reported. The median existing-home sales price increased slightly to $416,700. Declines in sales were seen in the midwest, south and west, though sales in the north-east held steady.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/12/home-sales-october-low\">Continue reading...</a>",
